  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">What a buyer asks before it prices anything</h2>
      <p class="reveal">A buyer is not only deciding whether the records are interesting. It has to satisfy itself that it can use them, which is a different question from whether your company holds them.</p>
      <ul class="checklist reveal">
        <li><strong>Can you transfer it?</strong>Whether the company can license these records to this buyer at all.</li>
        <li><strong>Can it be used for this purpose?</strong>Training, testing and commercial use are separate permissions.</li>
        <li><strong>Where did it come from?</strong>The system of record, how the export was made, and what rights attach to it.</li>
        <li><strong>How is personal data handled?</strong>The de-identification method and how it is checked, not just that names were removed.</li>
        <li><strong>What happens at the end?</strong>Whether copies are deleted or returned, and what becomes of models already trained.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">Why you go through us rather than direct</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Approaching an AI lab cold usually means an NDA, a long silence and one price with nothing to compare it to. We take the same dataset to several buyers, keep the negotiations and the confidentiality in one place, and bring back the terms. You only ever deal with buyers you have agreed to.</p>
